WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.110 --> 00:00:06.900
This is one of the most badass female characters
in Shounen of all time.

00:00:06.900 --> 00:00:12.730
Kugisaki Nobara has a violent fighting style,
is extremely expressive with her emotions

00:00:12.730 --> 00:00:18.040
and awesomely demonstrates that as a girl
you can be both, beautiful and strong at the

00:00:18.040 --> 00:00:22.870
same time. As the only female first year in
a team with two guys, it's anything but a

00:00:22.870 --> 00:00:27.780
surprise that many people have compared Kugisaki
with the character, that she shares quite

00:00:27.780 --> 00:00:30.950
a lot of these characteristics with, Sakura
from Naruto.

00:00:30.950 --> 00:00:35.590
However, while Sakura in many ways failed
to become the strong female role model that

00:00:35.590 --> 00:00:42.311
many wanted her to be, with Nobara Akutami
managed to create an awesome female character,

00:00:42.311 --> 00:00:48.030
that firmly stands side by side with Itadori
and Megumi, is incredibly strong-willed and

00:00:48.030 --> 00:00:54.250
is not merely reduced to being a love interest,
but in contrary is probably the most hard-boiled

00:00:54.250 --> 00:01:00.610
member of the trio. In other words, Kugisaki
is what Sakura was supposed to be. A strong

00:01:00.610 --> 00:01:12.780
female character that stands on equal ground
with the two male leads.

00:01:12.780 --> 00:01:18.210
This is accentuated by the fact, that Kugisaki,
just like Gojo is extremely self-centered

00:01:18.210 --> 00:01:24.659
and power-oriented. She actually shares a
quite similar character arc to her sensei.

00:01:24.659 --> 00:01:31.729
So, what exactly is Nobara's role in the story?
How strong is she really? Why do Maki and

00:01:31.729 --> 00:01:37.780
Mai have such an impact on her? And what is
her major flaw as a character?

00:01:37.780 --> 00:01:48.250
This is the story of Kugisaki Nobara.

00:01:48.250 --> 00:02:00.520
Kugisaki, despite being part of the main trio
in the story, has not really been assigned

00:02:00.520 --> 00:02:05.210
a proper purpose in the story yet. Something,
that Akutami does surprisingly often with

00:02:05.210 --> 00:02:10.220
characters he introduces. In many cases, their
role in the story only becomes clear much

00:02:10.220 --> 00:02:17.040
later, or in some cases, in true Togashi fashion,
the character simply remains a malleable wild

00:02:17.040 --> 00:02:22.950
card. Since this is an anime only analysis,
I won't give any examples, but the manga readers

00:02:22.950 --> 00:02:24.440
will know what I mean.

00:02:24.440 --> 00:02:30.840
Long story short, Nobara's role in the story,
both in the manga and the anime is quite unclear.

00:02:30.840 --> 00:02:35.330
She has escaped the pitiful fate of being
a mere love interest to the main character,

00:02:35.330 --> 00:02:40.629
and as Fushiguro and Itadori have a unusually
positive relationship, also doesn't have to

00:02:40.629 --> 00:03:03.349
play the role of moderator. She’s not someone
with a grand goal that we can follow like

00:03:03.349 --> 00:03:08.680
Maki, or someone driven by intense emotions
like Yuji or Megumi. In other words, Akutami

00:03:08.680 --> 00:03:13.849
still keeps Kugisaki's deeper role in the
story hidden, that as part of the main trio

00:03:13.849 --> 00:03:19.319
she will without any doubt get at some point,
while at the same time giving her an absolutely

00:03:19.319 --> 00:03:24.770
fantastic character arc and more and more
moments in the story to shine. So, first,

00:03:24.770 --> 00:03:34.470
you know what's up, let's take a closer look
at her character arc and powers.

00:03:34.470 --> 00:03:46.019
I would argue that Kugisaki, just like Fushiguro,
is actually already plenty strong even in

00:03:46.019 --> 00:03:51.379
the beginning of the story. And just like
Fushiguro and Itadori, Nobara also has a very

00:03:51.379 --> 00:03:57.069
interesting relation to death. Itadori is
scared of death, but is more than prepared

00:03:57.069 --> 00:04:02.680
to die to save someone else. Fushiguro generally
seems a bit to eager to sacrifice himself

00:04:02.680 --> 00:04:08.050
whenever he gets the chance. And Nobora, definitely
doesn't want to die either, but also isn't

00:04:08.050 --> 00:04:16.989
particularly scared of death. -

00:04:16.989 --> 00:04:21.299
She doesn't mind injuring herself, or even
dying, as long as she can pay her opponent

00:04:21.299 --> 00:04:26.819
back for it enough. Fittingly, her cursed
technique allows her to use nails and a straw

00:04:26.819 --> 00:04:32.719
doll to attack the opponent from distance,
inflicting pain and damage. She can also shoot

00:04:32.719 --> 00:04:37.379
the nails from a distance and thus influence
the environment around her.

00:04:37.379 --> 00:04:43.020
As a very self-righteous person, Nobara doesn’t
like it when good people get hurt, same as

00:04:43.020 --> 00:04:48.729
Yuji, same as Megumi, but when she sees herself
in the right she has no problem at all punishing

00:04:48.729 --> 00:04:58.099
what she calls a&nbsp;“bad” person.

00:04:58.099 --> 00:04:59.099
-

00:04:59.099 --> 00:05:03.120
The very first thing that becomes very obvious
to anyone who encounters Nobara for the first

00:05:03.120 --> 00:05:09.069
time, is her incredibly strong and straightforward
personality. Quite in the manner of many MALE

00:05:09.069 --> 00:05:14.129
Shounen characters, she wears her feelings
and thoughts right on her sleeve. When she

00:05:14.129 --> 00:05:24.309
is pissed, she says so. When she thinks something
is cute, she says so. When she is grateful,

00:05:24.309 --> 00:05:31.780
she says so. This straight-forwardness is
both a strength and a weakness. And the best

00:05:31.780 --> 00:05:40.449
scene to illustrate this central trait of
her character, is this one here.

00:05:40.449 --> 00:05:41.449
-

00:05:41.449 --> 00:05:46.099
You see, the irony here is not only that Nobara
has an attack called sympathy, where she inflicts

00:05:46.099 --> 00:05:51.000
pain on herself and her opponent, it's that
she has close to no sympathy or empathy in

00:05:51.000 --> 00:05:58.069
the first place. Which in a pretty messed
up way is absolutely hilarious. While both

00:05:58.069 --> 00:06:04.569
Itadori and Megumi suffer under the deep feelings
of empathy they have for others, it's the

00:06:04.569 --> 00:06:09.789
girl of the group that suffers from not having
enough of it. What a nice twist. To spell

00:06:09.789 --> 00:06:14.360
it out really quickly here, basically whenever
Kugisaki ends up in a situation that requires

00:06:14.360 --> 00:06:20.279
her to understand and relate to the feelings
of another person, she wildly and often violently

00:06:20.279 --> 00:06:28.719
rejects them. -

00:06:28.719 --> 00:06:34.190
To understand why, lets look at how nobara
approaches the central moral question of the

00:06:34.190 --> 00:06:39.979
story. What makes a good life worth living?
While both Itadori and Fushiguro make this

00:06:39.979 --> 00:06:46.810
about others, Kugisaki, much like Gojo makes
it mostly about herself. For her, living a

00:06:46.810 --> 00:06:51.939
good life means being able to express herself
freely, do what she likes and spend time with

00:06:51.939 --> 00:06:55.189
the few people she sees as worthy. -

00:06:55.189 --> 00:07:00.000
As always, I'm not saying that one is better
or more appropriate than the other. JuJutsu

00:07:00.000 --> 00:07:04.949
Kaisen kind of makes it a point, that most
of these characters have valid and understandable

00:07:04.949 --> 00:07:10.399
approaches to life. And for Nobara, escaping
the village she grew up in and moving to Tokyo

00:07:10.399 --> 00:07:15.839
ended up being her big goal, which was the
reason she became a sorcerer in the first

00:07:15.839 --> 00:07:29.089
place. Thus, Other than Yuji or Megumi she
has already reached her goal. As a result,

00:07:29.089 --> 00:07:33.869
her desire has now shifted from getting to
Tokyo, to preserving the live she has wished

00:07:33.869 --> 00:07:35.139
for and now gained.

00:07:35.139 --> 00:07:41.091
And the way she approaches it, is the same
as Gojo, strength. When you are strong, you

00:07:41.091 --> 00:07:46.659
can shape the world around you, do what you
want and keep those save that matter. Nobara

00:07:46.659 --> 00:07:52.179
thus constantly balances two personas, her
girly, feminine side, that is incredibly important

00:07:52.179 --> 00:07:57.719
to her, as well as being a strong sorcerer
and woman. This is wonderfully symbolized

00:07:57.719 --> 00:08:03.029
by her weapon, a hammer with a pink heart
on it. This duality of her character, that

00:08:03.029 --> 00:08:09.419
I personally find incredibly cool and well-executed,
is explored in great detail during her fight

00:08:09.419 --> 00:08:10.419
with momo.

00:08:10.419 --> 00:08:19.610
Momo holds the position that women in the
Jujutsu world have to be perfect in order

00:08:19.610 --> 00:08:24.789
to have a place in society. Perfect of Course
in the most conservative and rigid sense of

00:08:24.789 --> 00:08:34.990
the term. Now, I think you'll agree that Kugisaki
standing up against this idea, is a very important

00:08:34.990 --> 00:08:41.050
and impressive move. Yes, woman can be both,
strong and beautiful and you shouldn't let

00:08:41.050 --> 00:08:45.900
your life be determined by what society says.
Life is not a job and you should be able to

00:08:45.900 --> 00:08:47.300
be who you are.

00:08:47.300 --> 00:08:53.519
The thing that Nobara doesn't consider however
is, why Momo thinks so in the first place.

00:08:53.519 --> 00:08:58.199
Momo has experienced all the unfairness and
harsh expectations that her and the women

00:08:58.199 --> 00:09:03.190
around her have faced in the Jujutsu society.
She didn't come up with that view by herself,

00:09:03.190 --> 00:09:09.069
it's the conclusion she has drawn from the
suffering and struggle associated with being

00:09:09.069 --> 00:09:15.620
a female sorcerer. But Nobara doesn't get
it. No, not only does 't she get it, she doesn't

00:09:15.620 --> 00:09:29.300
want to get it. When Momo tries to explain
her thoughts, this is her reaction. - Not

00:09:29.300 --> 00:09:34.300
having any empathy is the major flaw of her
character.

00:09:34.300 --> 00:09:40.100
Just like Gojo, Kugisaki is extremely convinced
of herself and her worldview. While most other

00:09:40.100 --> 00:09:45.040
characters, like Itadori or Nanami for instance
don't have a lot of self-worth and are constantly

00:09:45.040 --> 00:09:51.769
doubtful about their own actions and decisions,
she sees herself as 100% righteous and 100%

00:09:51.769 --> 00:09:52.769
correct.

00:09:52.769 --> 00:09:58.750
And that is extremely ironic, because we know
that Nobara hates nothing more than people

00:09:58.750 --> 00:10:04.310
being judgey and full of predjudice, as happened
with her childhood friend Saori. And yet,

00:10:04.310 --> 00:10:09.829
there is almost no other character in JuJutsu
Kaisen that is as closed-minded as her. The

00:10:09.829 --> 00:10:21.170
very first time we meet her, the first thing
she does is impose herself on a modeling recruiter,

00:10:21.170 --> 00:10:26.110
which is especially funny because they are
seen as pretty creepy and pushy in Tokyo.

00:10:26.110 --> 00:10:31.300
So, Nobara immeaditley leaves a strong impression
by creeping out the creep, establishing her

00:10:31.300 --> 00:10:37.439
power and presence. Then, she proceeds to
judge both Megumi and Yuji within the first

00:10:37.439 --> 00:10:51.920
10 seconds of them meeting. - And she does
that with everyone. Even though she really

00:10:51.920 --> 00:10:56.459
wants to understand people she doesn't want
to actually listen to what people have to

00:10:56.459 --> 00:10:59.540
say and learn who they are.

00:10:59.540 --> 00:11:05.279
This becomes especially clear in her relationship
with Maki and Mai. Just like us viewers, the

00:11:05.279 --> 00:11:10.810
first impression Nobara gets is that Maki
is cool, confident and reliable, while Mai

00:11:10.810 --> 00:11:16.709
seems to be cold, manipulative and hateful.
In her own view, Maki is the good twin, and

00:11:16.709 --> 00:11:22.089
Mai is the evil twin. Kugisaki respects Maki
for her appearance as a strong woman, taking

00:11:22.089 --> 00:11:28.069
her as a role model. Mai meanwhile is evil
for taunting her sister for not having any

00:11:28.069 --> 00:11:39.160
powers. And once again, she thinks she’s
absolutely in the right because she’s defending

00:11:39.160 --> 00:11:44.860
her friend Maki that she likes against a person
she dislikes.

00:11:44.860 --> 00:11:50.610
Again she fails to understand that both Maki
and Mai are their own individual people with

00:11:50.610 --> 00:11:57.639
their own problems. Mai never wanted to become
a sorcerer, but simply wanted to have her

00:11:57.639 --> 00:12:05.300
sister, the only real family she had, by her
side. And that sister left her behind to defy

00:12:05.300 --> 00:12:11.759
their family. As we learn, Mai simply wants
attention from Maki. Maki of course has her

00:12:11.759 --> 00:12:17.720
own struggles and chose her own path, but
in the end she was the one who hurt Mai, not

00:12:17.720 --> 00:12:29.560
the other way around. - Someone else tries
to explain it to Nobara, but she tells Momo

00:12:29.560 --> 00:12:36.360
to shut up. And so, in the end, while she
is in the right when it comes to being a woman

00:12:36.360 --> 00:12:49.299
and thus wins against momo, she fails to emphasize
with Mai and ultimately looses the battle.

00:12:49.299 --> 00:12:50.299
-

00:12:50.299 --> 00:12:54.630
Why is that? Now, Even in the Manga, we know
surprisingly little about Nobara's past and

00:12:54.630 --> 00:12:59.819
how she grew up. We do know however, that
she always had a tendency to close herself

00:12:59.819 --> 00:13:02.480
off to others, no doubt to shield herself.

00:13:02.480 --> 00:13:08.560
Saying that Nobara doesn't feel empathy, does
not mean that she can't, but that she actively

00:13:08.560 --> 00:13:13.569
won't, since it makes her vulnerable. I think
she is very well aware of her own emotions.

00:13:13.569 --> 00:13:20.300
At her core, Nobara, just like Gojo really
really cares. So much in fact, that in the

00:13:20.300 --> 00:13:25.569
world of Jujutsu, where friends can be killed
any moment, she tries to to protect herself

00:13:25.569 --> 00:13:33.980
from experiencing that pain. We saw how she
reacted to Saori leaving town, almost as if

00:13:33.980 --> 00:13:44.439
she had passed away. The 
twist on her relationship with Saori was basically

00:13:44.439 --> 00:13:50.069
that she was just a normal girl, that Nobara
had a close relationship with and thus put

00:13:50.069 --> 00:13:55.509
up on a pedestal. Similarly we know that both
her and Megumi were in fact deeply hurt by

00:13:55.509 --> 00:14:04.240
Itadori apparently passing away.

00:14:04.240 --> 00:14:09.149
So her egocentric and un-empathetic approach
to life aren't that surprising. But over the

00:14:09.149 --> 00:14:10.949
course of her character arc, Kugisaki has
to learn to What Nobara needs to learn is

00:14:10.949 --> 00:14:15.990
to let her barriers down and just be more
open around other people, listen to what they

00:14:15.990 --> 00:14:21.029
have to say, and trusting that they’re not
going to just stomp all over her. She can

00:14:21.029 --> 00:14:26.580
remain a strong independent woman while at
the same time forming real relationships.

00:14:26.580 --> 00:14:30.800
And you can already see this happening as
well. Compare how Nobara acts in her first

00:14:30.800 --> 00:14:43.170
mission with Yuji, where she tires to do a
solo run, with the cursed womb arc, where

00:14:43.170 --> 00:14:58.760
she absolutely seamlessly fights in tandem
with Itadori. Character development. This

00:14:58.760 --> 00:15:04.449
is just an absolute exciting and fun female
character, and I can't wait to see what role

00:15:04.449 --> 00:15:07.079
she will play in the future of the story.

00:15:07.079 --> 00:15:12.759
While Kugisaki is defined by speaking her
mind, this guy here is known for speaking

00:15:12.759 --> 00:15:23.440
his favorite onigiri ingredients.
-

00:15:23.440 --> 00:15:27.880
And yet, he is one of the most interesting
and popular characters in the story, with

00:15:27.880 --> 00:15:33.399
one of the most fascinating powers. So, Make
sure to watch Inumaki's video ba clicking

00:15:33.399 --> 00:15:37.290
right here. Thanks for watching. Peace.

